<section>
  <h2>Open-source &amp; upstream</h2>
  <p>
    17 commits merged across five upstream projects, plus a
    <code>Reviewed-by</code> credit on another contributor&rsquo;s
    regulatory analysis.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>wpa_supplicant (hostap):</strong>
      <a href="https://git.w1.fi/cgit/hostap/log/?qt=author&amp;q=Kotze">seven
      commits merged</a> in July&ndash;August 2026 fixing Wi-Fi 7 multi-link
      (MLO) association: stale per-link BSS entries, ML-probe channel
      scanning, per-link key clearing, duplicated association-request IEs,
      and a PMKSA-caching deauthentication fallback &mdash; with two hwsim
      regression tests. Found and reproduced against real AP hardware;
      ships in the 2.13 release.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Linux kernel (mainline):</strong> authored the
      RTL8922AU USB RF-calibration fix
      (<a href="https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20260416045536.817930-1-loukot@gmail.com/">v3
      on lore</a>), with five independent <code>Tested-by</code> tags across
      USB WiFi chipsets. Also a
      <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20260414122728.92234-1-loukot@gmail.com/">cfg80211
      MLO group-key error-message fix</a>. Both now in mainline.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>NetworkManager:</strong> authored Wi-Fi 7 MLO awareness for
      the daemon&rsquo;s background-scan logic
      (<a href="https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/NetworkManager/NetworkManager/-/merge_requests/2405">MR
      !2405</a>, merged July 2026): parses the AP-MLD address from the
      Multi-Link element so a single-AP MLO association keeps the relaxed
      scan cadence, eliminating scan-induced traffic stalls. Landed after
      a five-revision review with the core maintainers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>wireless-regdb audit:</strong> seven regulatory-database
      commits merged across six jurisdictions (ZA, HK, RU, KR, UA, TG), each
      verified against the primary regulatory instrument (ICASA, OFCA, MSIT,
      SCRF, ETSI). Plus a <code>Reviewed-by</code> on a community-submitted
      RU 6 GHz 320 MHz patch &mdash; first review credit on someone else's
      regulatory analysis. Where the published instrument left a limit blank,
      I corresponded directly with the national regulator (ARCEP Burkina Faso)
      and obtained a written ruling on the applicable 6 GHz limits before
      writing the patch.
      <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/wireless-regdb/?q=f:loukot@gmail.com">Patch
      series on lore.</a> Includes an audit script for ongoing monitoring.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>morrownr/rtw89:</strong>
      <a href="https://github.com/morrownr/rtw89/pull/76">PR #76</a> backports
      the in-kernel RF-calibration fix to the out-of-tree DKMS driver
      (merged April 2026).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fedora bug 2458629:</strong>
      <a href="https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2458629">filed
      a reproducer and root-cause analysis</a> for a wpa_supplicant MLO
      reassociation race; assigned, in triage.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>In review:</strong> a cfg80211 patch improving the diagnostics
      when an association BSS lookup fails.
      <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/all/?q=f:loukot@gmail.com">All
      submissions on lore.</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
